Description: opengl/context: require swap_buffers param for FenceSync
 mpv 0.40 creates a GL fence for every frame rendered through the render API
 (vo_libmpv) and never deletes it, since only ra_gl_ctx_swap_buffers cleans
 them up and that isn't called there. On the Raspberry Pi's V3D driver every
 fence holds a sync_file descriptor, so a player using libmpv (Jellyfin
 Desktop) runs out of file descriptors after ~5 minutes of video and stops
 drawing.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/mpv-player/mpv/commit/f74adc4243
Bug: https://github.com/mpv-player/mpv/issues/17217
Applied-Upstream: 0.42.0
--- a/video/out/opengl/context.c
+++ b/video/out/opengl/context.c
@@ -232,7 +232,7 @@ bool ra_gl_ctx_submit_frame(struct ra_swapchain *sw, const struct vo_frame *fram
     if (p->opts->use_glfinish)
         gl->Finish();
 
-    if (gl->FenceSync) {
+    if (gl->FenceSync && p->params.swap_buffers) {
         GLsync fence = gl->FenceSync(GL_SYNC_GPU_COMMANDS_COMPLETE, 0);
         if (fence)
             MP_TARRAY_APPEND(p, p->vsync_fences, p->num_vsync_fences, fence);
